{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795828633,"nonce":"O/AkHQERQsbf6S8V/1Q8cCJnWaU=","message":"Fixed in ac316fc89a23ed7cd23d710fd5f04375021bfdac, by option 1: CSS semantics settle it.\n\nblinc_text adds LayoutOptions::word_spacing after each CSS word separator, and both measurers count separators the same way. TextMeasureContext carries it, and TextRenderingContext::prepare_text_with_style takes it.\n\nFound on the way: a text that does not wrap sized its box without its builder letter_spacing, so the box was narrower than the line. Fixed in the same commit.\n\nThe report said the CSS parser accepts word-spacing. It does not: there is no word-spacing case in blinc_css. That and RichText are filed separately.","files":null}]}